  "result": "Done and committed. `npm run fast` passes (biome, boundaries, tsc and the related tests).\n\n- **`src/cli/range.ts`:** `parseRange` turns `1-3,5` into `[1, 2, 3, 5]`. It trims whitespace and expands ranges inclusively. It throws `RangeError` on empty parts, non-numbers, open-ended parts like `1-` or `-2`, and reversed ranges like `3-1`.\n- **`test/cli/range.test.ts`:** node:test cases for the example, single numbers, whitespace and the invalid inputs.\n- **`scripts/lib/shard-weights.mjs`:** I added a weight entry for the new test file, because a repo rule test fails without one.\n- **`docs/notes-parse-range.md`:** the plan, written before the code and ticked off as I went.\n\nI didn't use a task id in the commit title, since you didn't give one and KRN-11 asks for one on managed work. The commit is local only and I haven't pushed it.",
